## Bill Line

One line of a Bill. A line is either an account line (`account` set, `sku` empty) or a product line (`sku` set):

- `account`: the expense or clearing account an account line debits;
- `sku`, `qty` (thousandths of a unit, so `48000000` is 48,000 lb), `unitCostMinor` (cents per unit) and `lot`: the product, quantity, cost and stock lot of a product line;
- `amountMinor`: the line amount in cents; for a product line it must equal `unitCostMinor × qty / 1000`, rounded;
- `debitAccount`: the account the line actually debits, the item's asset account for inventory;
- `description`, `cls`, `loc`: label and dimension tags.

```ts
import { BillLine } from '@cardstack/catalog/cards/accounting/ledger-cards';
```

Bill holds `lines = containsMany(BillLine)` and debits `debitAccount` (or `account` when that is empty) for each line with a positive amount. `Bill.post` enforces the amount and account rules above.

### Non-goals
No per-line tax or discount. Amounts are integer cents (`…Minor` fields) with no currency field; the ledger is single-currency.

### Example
A green-coffee product line received into lot `HUI-2026-03` and debited to inventory `1200`.
